title start
Layout plan
title end

paragraph start
name: paragraph-layout-goal
Goal. The master view shows boxes inside boxes. Where each box
sits is written in layout files, never inside the content
files. Shape builds every layout by hand. Nothing arranges
itself.
paragraph end


paragraph start
name: paragraph-layout-decided-rules
Decided. A layout file only says which files appear in its box
and where. It holds no content. Positions are relative to the
box. Links are by name and never by position. A layout can nest
another layout as a box. Version one stays tiny.
paragraph end

paragraph start
name: paragraph-layout-decided-modular
Decided. Layouts are modular. One file may appear in many
layouts. There is no hard-coded layout and no switch. The page
reads every layout in the notation folder and draws them all
combined. Layouts only combine, they never replace each other.
paragraph end

paragraph start
name: paragraph-layout-decided-one-card
Decided. One card per file. All layouts merge into one map. A
link arrow attaches to the one card of its file.
paragraph end

paragraph start
name: paragraph-layout-decided-no-fight
Decided. Layouts can never error or fight each other. A file
placed twice takes the spot from the fixed order of layout name,
then line order, and the other placement is ignored silently. A
loop of nested layouts is skipped at the repeat. A line naming a
missing file is skipped. Two cards on one spot: the later card
moves to the next free spot. The order by layout name is a pick
that Shape may change.
paragraph end

paragraph start
name: paragraph-layout-decided-syntax
Decided. A layout is written like all other notation: a block
with start and end lines and declarations inside. It reuses
declarations the parser already knows, so the parser needs no
change. Shape: a layout block with a name, holding card blocks
and box blocks. A card has a target file. A box has a target
layout. Both have a place of x y. The block types are layout,
card and box, in both blocktypes folders.
paragraph end

paragraph start
name: paragraph-layout-decided-caption
Decided. Every layout, card and box may carry a caption, which
is its description. The map shows it under the title. A box
caption on a nested box wins over the caption of its layout.
paragraph end

paragraph start
name: paragraph-layout-confirmed
Confirmed on screen. Link blocks are indexed. The index holds a
layout-item record per layout, card and box. Nested boxes are
drawn from them, with files in no layout in a row below.
paragraph end



paragraph start
name: paragraph-layout-inspiration
Ideas to borrow. Obsidian Canvas: layout is its own file. C4
model: boxes inside boxes with zoom levels. D2 and Graphviz
clusters: nested containers written in text. Maps of content:
one note that only lists and arranges others.
paragraph end







paragraph start
name: paragraph-layout-decided-fallback
Decided. A file in no layout is still drawn in a wrapped row, so
no file is hidden.
paragraph end

paragraph start
name: paragraph-layout-decided-home-scope
Decided. Layout files and the settings file live in AIU NOTATION/
notation/layouts, beside blocktypes and types. Never in demo and
never in a .notation folder. The master view has a folder scope,
the scope key of the settings block, now demo/. Files outside it stay in the
index and are never deleted.
paragraph end

paragraph start
name: paragraph-layout-decided-settings
Decided. Sizes, spacing and the arrow curve live in a settings
block in notation/layouts/layout-settings.aiu. Keys: width,
height, gap, stepx, stepy, margin, pad, head, curve, scope, padv, padh, titlesize, descsize, labelsize. Curve is 0
to 1, 0.5 is the old look. Settings blocks merge in file and line
order, later wins. Missing or bad keys keep the old defaults.
paragraph end

paragraph start
name: paragraph-layout-decided-tap
Decided. First tap on a card lights it and the cards it links to
and dims the rest. A second tap on the lit card opens the file. A
tap on empty space clears the focus. Phones send a fake mouse
click after a touch, so the page ignores mouse taps within 800 ms
of a touch tap.
paragraph end

paragraph start
name: paragraph-layout-decided-big-demo
Decided. The demo folder holds 5 folders (ideas, people, places,
tools, events) of 24 pages each, with 2 to 3 links per page, some
across folders. One layout per folder, and layout-demo-world
holds the 5 boxes. Generated once, then edited by hand.
paragraph end

paragraph start
name: paragraph-layout-state
State. Confirmed on screen: boxes, descriptions and arrows look
right. Written, not yet confirmed on screen: settings read from
notation, focus on tap with the double tap guard, and the big
demo.
paragraph end



paragraph start
name: paragraph-layout-decided-settings-tui
Decided. Settings are edited in a TUI, never by hand in code. The
file is AIU ECOSYSTEM/ecosystem/ecosystem TUI configuration/settings-tui.rkt. It reads
and writes notation/layouts/layout-settings.aiu, tells the server
to reload after every change, and takes every color from the theme
engine only. One box per group: cards, arrows, spacing, text,
scope.
paragraph end

paragraph start
name: paragraph-layout-open
Open, in this order. 1. Settings TUI as a ecosystem command.
2. Zoom levels: far shows box
titles, close shows cards. 3. Table view as a second reading of
the same index. 4. Descriptions for plain files in no layout.
paragraph end

paragraph start
name: paragraph-layout-decided-zoom
Decided. Zoom has two levels. Below the zoomcut setting, a
percent, the map hides cards and arrows and shows only box
titles and descriptions. At or above it, cards show. A tap on
a hidden card does nothing. Far, a box title keeps a constant screen size but never wider than its box, and hides if unreadable. Only boxes with no box inside show a description, and only if it fits. The default is 50.
paragraph end

paragraph start
name: paragraph-layout-decided-far-layout
Decided. Far zoom has its own layout, sized in screen pixels.
A box with only cards shrinks to one small box for its title.
A box with boxes inside sizes its cells from the largest inner
box, so no empty space is left. Far layout is recomputed in
zoom steps of 15 percent. Files in no layout are hidden far.
paragraph end

paragraph start
name: paragraph-layout-decided-far-packing
Decided. Far layout packs tight. Each grid column and row has its
own size, empty ones are dropped. A leaf box is sized from its
title and description, not a fixed size.
paragraph end

paragraph start
name: paragraph-layout-decided-smooth-zoom
Decided. Zoom eases to a target zoom, anchored on the fingers.
Wheel and pinch are less sensitive. Near and far layouts are two
layers that crossfade in a band of 30 percent around the cutoff.
When the far layout re-flows at a zoom step, the old far layer
fades out while the new one fades in.
paragraph end

paragraph start
name: paragraph-layout-decided-zoom-settings
Decided. The settings TUI has a zoom box: zoomcut, zoomband,
zoomease, zoomwheel. The website reads all four. The cursor
follows the screen order, so zoomcut can be selected.
paragraph end
